      {
        "kind": "kpis",
        "summary": "The documented measurement angle is a per-channel performance breakdown; no vendor uplift figures are provided.",
        "status": "documented",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Demand Gen reports performance broken down by channel, which you can review to guide campaign optimization.",
            "status": "documented",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "source_id": "google.demand_gen.channels",
                "source_url": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15973205?hl=en",
                "locator": "What are channel controls?",
                "source_site": "Google Ads Help",
                "source_title": "Demand Gen channel controls",
                "raw_sha256": null,
                "cleaned_sha256": null
              }
            ],
            "conditions": []
          },
          {
            "text": "A useful metric to watch is channel-level cost and conversion performance (e.g., conversions or cost per conversion per channel from the channel breakdown): if you restrict to a channel like YouTube Shorts, delivery shifts to that surface, so per-channel results show the reallocation. Trade-off: narrower channel selection reduces total inventory, which can raise costs even as fit improves.",
            "status": "inferred",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "source_id": "google.demand_gen.channels",
                "source_url": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15973205?hl=en",
                "locator": "What are channel controls?",
                "source_site": "Google Ads Help",
                "source_title": "Demand Gen channel controls",
                "raw_sha256": null,
                "cleaned_sha256": null
              },
              {
                "source_id": "google.demand_gen.channels",
                "source_url": "https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/15973205?hl=en",
                "locator": "How to use channel controls in Demand Gen",
                "source_site": "Google Ads Help",
                "source_title": "Demand Gen channel controls",
                "raw_sha256": null,
                "cleaned_sha256": null
              }
            ],
            "conditions": [
              "The mechanism is channel-level performance reporting; any uplift is conditional on your own before/after comparison, not guaranteed by Google."
            ]
          }
        ]
